      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first European‑American settlers arrived in the late 1850s, with Neal McDonald patenting 240 acres on July 1, 1859.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bismarck_arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bismarck United Methodist Church, founded in 1885, remains a historic landmark listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
